  FT["BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014"] = {"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-09","articleCount":28,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":null,"en":"TOWN PLANNERS REGISTRATION ORDER 2014","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","docNumber":"S 40/2014","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","promulgatedDate":"2014","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014.pdf》（13 页），本次切分 28 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"(1) This Order may be cited as the Town Planners Registration Order, 2014 and shall commence on a date to be appointed by the Minister, with the approval the SuHan and Yang Di-Pertuan, by notification in the Gazette.\n\n(2) The long title of this Order is \"An Order to provide for the registration of town planners and for purposes connected therewith or incidental thereto\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"text":{"en":"In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires - member\" means a member of the Board appointed under 3(2){b) or {c); means the Board of Town Planners established by section 3(1); of registration\" means a certificate of registration issued under means the chairman of the Board; means the Minister charged with the responsibility for town planning matters; means the town planning profession; means the Register of Town Planners referred to in section 12; means the Registrar of Town Planners referred to in section 11.\n\nOF TOWN PLANNERS Establishment and constitution of Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"{ 1) is hereby established a board known as the Board of Town\n\n(2) The Board shall consist of the following members - {a} the Commissioner for Town and Country Planning, who shall be the chairman; {b) 4 persons appointed by the Minister who are town planners or who are members of Royal Town Planning Institute of the United or any other internationally recognised professional body approved by the Minister; {c) one person appointed by the Minister from locally recognised professional bodies approved by the Minister.\n\n(3) The period of appointment of members, other than the chairman, shall be 3 years, but such members shall be eligible for re-appointment. {4) by the Board shall, notwithstanding any vacancy in the or that it is afterwards discovered that there was a defect in the of any person purporting to be a member thereof, be as valid as if no such vacancy or defect had existed. of Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"{1) In the absence of the chairman from a meeting of the Board, the present shall elect from amongst themselves a person to be the for that meeting.\n\n(2) The chairman of a meeting shall have an original vote and also a casting vote.\n\n(3) meet at such places and times as the chairman may appoint and, at a meeting, 4 members shall form a quorum.\n\n(4) the provisions of this Order, the Board may determine its own procedure. of appointment."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The appointment of an appointed member of the Board shall terminate if he resigns his office. of appointment."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The Minister may revoke the appointment of an appointed member of the {a} if his conduct, whether in connection with his duties as a member of the Board or otherwise, has been such as to bring discredit to the Board; {b} if he has become incapable of properly carrying out his duties as a of the Board; {c} if he has been convicted on a charge in respect of(i) an offence involving fraud, dishonesty or moral turpitude;\n\n(ii) an offence under any law relating to corruption;\n\n(iii) any offence under this Order; or\n\n(iv) any other offence punishable with imprisonment exceeding 2 years; {d} if he has been adjudicated bankrupt; {e} if he has been found or declared to be of unsound mind or has become incapable of managing his affairs; ({} if he absents himself from 3 consecutive meetings of the Board obtaining leave in writing from the chairman; {g} if his registration has been cancelled or has become void; or {h) if his name has been removed from the Register. of Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"The functions of the Board are{a} to approve or reject applications for registration under this Order;\n\n(b) to recommend to the Minister the scale of fees to be charged by registered town planners for professional advice and services rendered; (c} to establish, maintain, develop and improve the standards of professional conduct and ethics of the profession;\n\n(d) to regulate the conduct of the town planning profession; (e} to hear and determine itself or to appoint an arbitrator to hear disputes relating to the professional conduct and ethics of registered town\n\n(f) to represent the profession in any matter in which it may be necessary or expedient;\n\n(g) to examine, report and make recommendations any other matters affecting the profession;\n\n(h) to appoint a person to represent it on a body or panel of examiners which may be appointed by any body representing the profession; (i} to make recommendations to the relevant authority relating to any examination for qualification for admission to the profession; (j} to appoint members of the Board to sit on a board, committee or body formed for any purpose affecting the profession; (k} to appoint members of the Board to sit on the board of another professional body;\n\n(l) to produce, publish and sell planning bulletins or newsletters; and\n\n(m) generally, to do all such acts, matters and things as it considers necessary to carry out the provisions of this Order."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Board may appoint committees as it thinks expedient\n\n(a) to advise it on matters concerning its functions, powers and duties;\n\n(b) for the proper discharge of its functions, the exercise of its powers and the performance of its duties;\n\n(c) for any purpose arising out of or connected with its functions, powers and duties; {d} to carry out its functions, powers or duties as it may determine or\n\n(e) to carry out investigations upon any complaint made against any registered town planner.\n\n(2) Subject to this Order and to any directions given by the Board, a committee may regulate its own procedure. to report to Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"text":{"en":"(1) A committee shall report its findings and make recommendations to the\n\n(2) Upon receiving the findings and recommendations, the Board mayfa) accept the findings and recommendations of a committee and make the recommended order;\n\n(b) refer the matter back to a committee for further inquiry; or\n\n(c) make such other order as the Board thinks fit. of meeting."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"chapter":{"en":"PART II"},"heading":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE ----------------"},"text":{"en":"A committee shall cause(a) minutes of its meetings to be kept and maintained in proper form; and\n\n(b) copies of such minutes to be forwarded to the Board not later than 2 weeks from the date of the meeting.\n\nOF TOWN PLANNERS and duties of Registrar."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) The Commissioner for Town and Country Planning shall be the\n\n(2) The Registrar shall -\n\n(a) keep and maintain the Register; {b) sign all certificates of registration and record in the Register all of registration, cancellation, suspension and reinstatement; {c) publish in the Gazette(i) as soon as practicable after 1st January each year, a list the names, addresses, qualifications and dates of qualification of all registered town planners; and\n\n(ii) from time to time, a list containing the names, addresses, and dates of qualification of registered town who have been - (aa) added; (ab) from; or .(ac) reinstated into, the Register;\n\n(d) publish in planning bulletins or newsletters a list containing the and addresses of registered town planners who have beenli)\n\n(ii) from; or\n\n(iii) reinstated into, within one month of such addition, removal or reinstatement. !3) In any proceedings(a) the publication of a list under subsection (2) shall be prima facie that persons whose names appear therein are registered town\n\n(b) a certificate issued pursuant to section 16 shall be prima facie that the person named therein as a town planner is a registered town planner; and\n\n(c) a certificate under the hand of the Registrar that the name of a has been entered, added, removed from or reinstated into the Register shall be conclusive evidence that that person is or is not (as the case may be) a registered town planner. (4} The Registrar may publish annually and offer for sale copies of the"}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"{ 1) of Town Planners shall contain the names and addresses and such other particulars, if any, as are prescribed of all persons who are registered in accordance with this Order.\n\n(2) The Registrar shall keep and maintain the Register at the office of the which shall be accessible for public inspection. town planners."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) No person shall, unless he is registered, take or use the name or title of town planner or arty other word in any language having the same or a similar or being to the like intent or take or use any other name, title, emblem or description implying that his name or the name of any person employed by him is registered or that he or such other person is entitled to be registered.\n\n(2) A person who acts in contravention of subsection (1) is guilty of an and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and to a further fine of $100 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction. eligible for registration."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Subject to this Order the following persons are eligible to be registered - (a} any person employed as a town planner at the date of of this Order;\n\n(b) any person who is a member of Royal Town Planning Institute of the United Kingdom or any other internationally recognised professional town planning or who is a holder of such other qualification as the Minister may declare by notification in the Gazette to be an approved qualification for the purposes of this section, who has complied with such conditions as the Board may determine. for registration."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) Any person eligible for registration under this Order may apply to the Board for registration. !2) Every application made to the Board shall be accompanied by a nonrefundable application fee of a prescribed amount which shall be paid in the specified by the Board and in such form and manner as the Board may of certificates of registration."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) The Registrar shall issue to any town planner whose application for registration has been approved by the Board, a certificate of registration in a form by the Board upon payment of the prescribed fee.\n\n(2) The certificate shall -\n\n(a) expire on the 31st December of the year in which it was issued; and\n\n(b) be renewable annually upon payment of the prescribed fee."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"( 1) Every registered town planner shall be entitled to -\n\n(a) prepare planning schemes for the purposes of the Town and Country Planning (Development Control) Act (Chapter 143);\n\n(b) carry out urban, rural and regional development planning studies, and feasibility and environmental impact assessment studies relating to land use;\n\n(c) prepare and submit applications for planning permission, subdivision layouts, drawings, planning reports, planning briefs and development proposals to any person or public authority for the purposes of developing any land; and\n\n(d) any other work relating to town and country planning.\n\n(2) Nothing contained in this section shall affect the entitlement of any person under any other written law to do any of the things mentioned in subsection ( 1). of change of address."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Every registered town planner shall notify the Registrar of any change in his business address or correspondence address within 14 days of such change. from Register."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"The Registrar shall remove from the Register the name and other particulars town planner who - {a) has died; {b) has failed to renew his registration within 3 months of its expiry; {c) has been registered through an error as to his qualification for {d) who has applied in writing for such removal. of Board to cancel certificate and remove name from Register."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"(1) Subject to this section, the Board may direct that a certificate be and the name and other particulars of a registered town planner be removed from the Register if - {a) he has been convicted of an offence involving fraud or dishonesty; {b) he has been adjudged bankrupt; {c) he becomes of unsound mind; {d) he has been convicted of an offence under this Order; {e) his registration has been obtained by fraud or misrepresentation; {f) his qualification for registration under section 12 has been or cancelled by the authority through which it was acquired or by which it was awarded; {g) he has been found guilty of an improper act or conduct which renders him, in the opinion of the Board, unfit to be a town planner; or {h) it appears to the Board that he is unable to carry out the duties of a town planner effectively in Brunei Darussalam.\n\n(2) No direction shall be given under subsection {1} unless the Board has the registered town planner to whom it relates an opportunity of being heard either personally or by counsel.\n\n(3) A direction under subsection (1) shall not take effect until the expiration month from the date on which it has been communicated to the registered town planner to whom it relates or, where an appeal against the direction has been made to the Minister under section 23, until the appeal has been determined or withdrawn.\n\n(4) Where a direction under subsection (J) takes effect, the Registrar shall make such alteration in the Register as is necessary to give effect to it. of certificate of registration."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"A person whose name has been removed from the Register shall surrender to the certificate of registration within 14 days of notification of such"}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Where the name has been removed from the Register under section 19(b), it shall be reinstated forthwith upon payment of the prescribed fee."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Any person aggrieved by any decision of the Board under this Order may the Minister, whose decision shall be finaL"}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"A town planner in public office shall be exempted from payment of any fee pursuant to this Order. Fraudulent registration."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Any person who, in an application for registration under this Order, makes, produces or causes to be made or produced, any false on fraudulent representation, certificate or declaration, either verbally or in writing, or who or assists therein is guilty of an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or both. 14th. 2014"}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with any provision of this for which no other penalty is expressly provided is guilty of an offence and on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000, imprisonment for a term not year or both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day during which the offence continues after No action in absence of bad faith."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"No action or proceeding shall lie against the Board, any committee or any thereof for any act or thing done or omitted to be done in good faith in the discharge or purported discharge of its or his duties under this Order."}},{"id":"BN-S-40-2014-TOWN-PLANNERS-REGISTRATION-ORDER-2014-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28."},"chapter":{"en":"PART III"},"text":{"en":"{1) The Minister may, with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and make rules which are necessary or expedient for giving effect to and carrying out the provisions of this Order, including the prescription of fees and of any other thing required to be or which may be prescribed under this and for the due administration thereof. {2) Such rules may include such incidental, and supplementary provisions as the Minister considers necessary or expedient. day of Rejab, 1435 Hijriah corresponding to the 6th. day of May, 2014 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM"}}],"pack":"bn-p16"};
